! Gosper's Hack is an efficient method of computing the next higher
! integer with the same number of set bits (Hamming weight). It was
! invented by Bill Gosper. The algorithm is widely used in combinatorics
! for enumerating combinations.
! 
! Task
! 
! Write a function or procedure to compute the next higher integer with
! the same number of set bits as a given positive integer, using Gosper’s
! Hack.
! 
! Show the result of applying it ten times to each of the numbers 1, 3, 7,
! and 15.
! 
! Reference
! 
! -   Gosper's Hack explained


